<title>ITALY: FORECAST - Italy seen issuing 16.25 trln lire Bot.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Italy seen issuing 16.25 trln lire Bot.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury is seen issuing about 16.25 trillion lire of short-term bills (Bot) at its mid-month auction against some 17.0 trillion lire maturing, according to the average from a Reuter poll of analysts.</p>
<p>Analysts' Bot forecasts range from 16.0 trillion lire to 16.75 trillion lire. The Treasury is also seen issuing a new tranche of some 2.5 trillion lire of zero coupon certificates (CTZ).</p>
<p>The Treasury will announce the amounts it will offer at auction on Monday. The auction date is set for Thursday, October 10 with settlement on Tuesday, October 15.</p>
<p>Following are the analysts' forecasts:</p>
<p>			   3-Mo Bot    6-Mo Bot   1-Yr Bot Tot Bot CTZ</p>
<p>    Maturing	   5.0	     5.5	  6.5    17.0    2.5</p>
<p>============================================================</p>
<p>    Bank of America  4.75	    5.25	 6.5    16.5    2.5</p>
<p>    Banca di Roma    4.75	    5.0	  6.5    16.25   2.5</p>
<p>    Caboto	     5.0	     5.25	 6.5    16.75   2.5</p>
<p>    Chase Manhattan  4.5	     5.0	  6.5    16.0    2.5</p>
<p>    BCI		  5.0	     5.25	 6.25   16.5    2.5</p>
<p>    Credito Italiano 5.0	     5.25	 6.0    16.25   2.5</p>
<p>    Prometeia	  4.5	     5.25	 6.5    16.25  *4.5</p>
<p>	     * Forecast for entire month of October</p>
<p>============================================================</p>
<p>    Consensus	  4.75	    5.00	 6.25   16.25   2.5</p>
<p>---Milan newsroom ++392 66101399</p>
